Parameters describe the values a function needs.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    greet |name String, excited Bool| {
        if excited {
            io.line([: Hello, [name]!])
        }
    }
]

Each parameter has a name and a type.

A default lets the caller omit an argument. The parameter keeps its declared type.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    describe |prefix String = "item", subject String| -> String {
        return [prefix, ": ", subject]
    }

    label = describe(subject = "apple")
]

The call supplies `subject` by name and keeps the default prefix.

Write an empty argument list when you call a function that has no parameters. A directive with no operands takes its bare name.
